        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: die Einigung",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "die Einigung — \"the agreement (that is reached)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Nach drei Stunden kamen sie endlich zu einer Einigung. After three hours they finally reached an agreement."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Plural: die Einigungen. It belongs with sich einigen — to come to an agreement."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Einigung is the noun of sich einigen, from einig \"at one, united\", built on ein \"one\", inherited from Proto-Germanic ainaz (EtymDB): two sides become one."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
