          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: einerseits",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "einerseits — \"on the one hand\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Einerseits ist die Wohnung schön, auf der anderen Seite ist sie sehr teuer. On the one hand the flat is nice; on the other, it is very expensive."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "An adverb: the verb comes right after it, einerseits ist …. It usually has a partner later in the sentence, such as auf der anderen Seite or aber."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "einerseits is built from ein \"one\" and Seite \"side\", inherited from Old High German sīta and Proto-Germanic sīdōn (EtymDB), with the adverb ending -s: on one side."
            }
          ]
        },
